        <h1>LeetCode 3498: Reverse Degree of a String (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Given a string s, calculate its reverse degree. For each character, assign a value equal to
                26 minus its position in the alphabet (so 'a' is worth 26, 'z' is worth 1). Multiply each
                character's value by its 1-indexed position in the string, then sum all of these products to
                get the reverse degree. Return the reverse degree of s.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: s = "abc"<br>
                Output: 148<br>
                Explanation: 'a' contributes 26*1=26, 'b' contributes 25*2=50, and 'c' contributes 24*3=72,
                giving a total of 148.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int reverseDegree(string str) {
        int result = 0;
        for (int idx = 0; idx &lt; str.size(); idx++) {
            int score = 26 - (str[idx] - 'a');
            result += score * (idx + 1);
        }
        return result;
    }
};</code></pre>
